AuroraSetViewDelta: move the world view of a repaint, in the GX command stream

The native port's 60 fps mode (docs/FPS60_PLAN.md, step B) repaints each game frame's draw lists a
second time (paint B) with the camera halfway between two game frames. The lists hold view-space
matrices (J3D bakes the view into its draw matrices in the draw pass) as well as packets that load the
view at paint time, so the view is changed where everything meets: in the uniform Aurora builds per
draw.

- GX_AURORA_SET_VIEW_DELTA (0x0051), written by AuroraSetViewDelta(delta, projFrom, projTo): a u8
  (0 = off) and, when on, a 3x4 rigid transform C, the perspective projection it applies to and the
  projection to draw instead (six floats each, GXSetProjection's encoding). It is a command in the
  stream, so with the FIFO worker (ProcessingMode::Thread, and patch 0018's asynchronous end of frame)
  it applies exactly to the draws written after it, whenever the worker translates them.
- fill_uniform (shader_info.cpp): while on, a draw whose projection is perspective and equal to
  projFrom gets every position matrix premultiplied by C, every normal matrix by C's rotation, light
  positions by C and light directions by its rotation (GX lights are given in view space), and projTo
  as its projection. Orthographic draws and other perspective projections are untouched. The state is
  GXState::viewDelta; turning it on or off marks the uniform dirty; clear_draw_cache (the end of
  every frame) turns it off.

Off (never called), nothing changes: one bool tested per uniform build.

